     2| * IVX Autonomous Run Log — PERMANENT per-run evidence persistence (2026-07-26).
     3| *
     4| * WHY THIS EXISTS:
     5| *   The scheduler state file (`scheduler/state.json`) only records the LAST run
     6| *   per job kind (a single `runCount` + `lastSummary`). Hundreds of runs
     7| *   completed with no per-run evidence artifact — `runsWithoutEvidence: 556`
     8| *   vs `runsWithEvidence: 11`. This module closes that gap permanently.
     9| *
    10| * WHAT IT DOES:
    11| *   Persists EVERY autonomous engine/scheduler run as an individual, permanent,
    12| *   append-only record in the Supabase-backed durable event store. Each record
    13| *   carries the full evidence envelope: job id, worker id, engine, start/finish
    14| *   time, status, runtime, records discovered/inserted/updated, errors, source
    15| *   URLs, evidence artifact, commit SHA, deployment SHA.
    16| *
    17| * DURABILITY:
    18| *   Records are stored via `appendDurableEvent` into the `ivx_durable_events`
    19| *   Postgres table (Supabase). They survive server restarts, Render redeploys,
    20| *   and scheduler restarts. When Supabase is not configured (local dev/tests),
    21| *   records fall back to the local filesystem append-only JSONL log.
    22| *
    23| * HONESTY:
    24| *   - A run record is written for EVERY run, ok or failed, evidenced or empty.
